  "summary_en": "Law journal article arguing that violating robots.txt, the web-crawler exclusion standard, can ground civil liability in common law jurisdictions through unilateral contract and tort (trespass to chattels, negligence). It includes an empirical study of robots.txt changes on the top 200 websites after ChatGPT. The 'robots' are software crawlers, not physical robots.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Robots.txt can form a unilateral contract when a bot accesses a site.",
   "Robots.txt serves as notice sufficient for tortious liability, including negligence.",
   "Civil liability is preferable to criminal or copyright remedies for scraping.",
   "Top-200 site analysis shows growing bans on AI crawlers such as GPTBot.",
   "Clarifying liability helps counter internet fragmentation."
